      "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith encoder disaggregation (EPD), a tokens-in multimodal request (`input_ids` plus `image_data`, no text) fails on the language server with HTTP 500 when the scheduler assembles the multimodal inputs. The `zmq_to_scheduler` and `mooncake` transfer backends and the gRPC zmq receiver all use this scheduler-side path. This affects a default EPD launch, because `--encoder-transfer-backend auto` picks `zmq_to_scheduler` for every model except Kimi-K3 with TP > 1. The scheduler stores `input_ids` as `array(\"q\")`. A tokens-in request has no text (`None` over HTTP, `\"\"` from the gRPC servicer), so the scheduler gives this array to the processor as the prompt. The shared base processor, which Qwen3-VL uses, reads a `list` prompt as token IDs and any other prompt as text, so the HF tokenizer gets the array as text and rejects it. #32541 added this fallback to `input_ids` without the `list()` conversion that the tokenized-input branch already has. `zmq_to_tokenizer` is not affected, because the tokenizer side already passes a list. This PR makes the scheduler side do the same.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Scheduler-side EPD prompt selection converts `input_ids` to `list[int]` before it gives them to the processor.\n- Text-in requests and processors that set `prefer_tokenized_input` keep the same behavior.\n- A new unit test checks that a tokens-in prompt reaches the processor as a list, for `input_text=None` (HTTP) and `input_text=\"\"` (gRPC).\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n`Qwen/Qwen3-VL-2B-Instruct`, encoder-only and language-only servers on one GPU, `zmq_to_scheduler`, temperature 0:\n\n| Request | main (`450837e770`) | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Tokens-in | HTTP 500 `Failed to assemble multimodal inputs: text input must be of type str ...` | HTTP 200, 1041 prompt tokens, correct image description. Same text and token count as `zmq_to_tokenizer`. |\n| Text-in | HTTP 200 | HTTP 200 |\n\nThe E2E run covers `zmq_to_scheduler` only. `mooncake` and the gRPC zmq receiver call the same function, but I did not run them end to end.\n\nUnit tests: `test_encode_receiver.py` passes 9/9. Both subtests of the new test fail on main.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNot applicable. The change adds one `list()` copy of `input_ids` each time the scheduler assembles a multimodal request.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Format code with pre-commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#format-code-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests according to the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests).\n- [ ] Update documentation according to [Write documentations](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#write-documentations).\n- [ ] Provide accuracy and speed benchmark results according to [Test the accuracy](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#test-the-accuracy) and [Benchmark the speed](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#benchmark-the-speed).\n- [x] Follow the SGLang code style [guidance](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-style-guidance).\n\n## Review and Merge Process\n\n1. Ping Merge Oncalls to start the process. See the [PR Merge Process](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/MAINTAINER.md#pull-request-merge-process).\n2. Get approvals from [CODEOWNERS](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.github/CODEOWNERS) and other reviewers.\n3. Trigger CI tests with [comments](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#how-to-trigger-ci-tests) or contact authorized users to do so.\n   - Common commands include `/tag-and-rerun-ci`, `/tag-run-ci-label`, `/rerun-failed-ci`\n4. After green CI and required approvals, ask Merge Oncalls or people with Write permission to merge the PR.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:no_entry_sign: [Run #38821699947](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38821699947)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #38821699986](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38821699986)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #38821699997](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/38821699997)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n<!-- pr-states:end -->\n\n",
